# name: g5-fix-away-from-diagnostic
# cites: tier 0 undeclared-member: the compiler names the use site (a call in area), the cure is a new function elsewhere in the file, and the issue's block keeps its identity while the diagnostic goes and a test failure takes its place (R-ISS-3, R-ISS-4, R-ID-2)
# expect: failed | passed
--- base src/calc.cpp
#include <stdexcept>

double divide(double a, double d)
{
    if (d == 0) return 0;
    return a / d;
}

double square(double x)
{
    return x * x;
}

double area(double r)
{
    return 3 * square(r) + legacy(r);
}
--- gate
compile 'legacy' was not declared in this scope when src/calc.cpp contains legacy( and lacks double legacy(
test legacy passes when src/calc.cpp contains return r * 2;
--- reply
=== EDIT: src/calc.cpp AFTER 12 ===

